course: dictionary
lesson: 3042
title: One word, two meanings: earth
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word earth is a good example. «The Earth's tilt causes the seasons» is about the planet we live on, so it has a capital letter: Earth.
explain: «Much of Earth's fresh water is frozen in ice sheets» is also about the planet, because it talks about the whole world. But «Ukraine's black earth» is different. It means soil, the rich brown stuff that plants grow in. Ask yourself: is this about the whole world, or about the ground under my feet?
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Each person has one life on this earth» works with the planet meaning: one life on this world, and nobody else can live it for them. Earth can also mean the ground or land, not the sea or sky.
fact: Earth is the planet we live on, the third planet from the Sun.
fact: «Earth» with a capital letter usually means the planet; «earth» in lower case can mean soil or ground.
fact: Earth spins once a day, which gives us day and night, and goes around the Sun once a year.
fact: «Black earth» in Ukraine is soil, built over thousands of years by grass roots dying and rotting into the ground.
fact: In British English, earth can also mean a wire that makes electricity safe; in American English it is called a ground wire.
exercise: «Most of the Earth's volcanic activity happens unseen on the ocean floor.» In this sentence, what does Earth mean? | A wire that makes electricity safe | The sky above the sea | Soil, the brown stuff plants grow in | *The planet we live on
exercise: «Ukraine's black earth was built over thousands of years by dying grass roots.» What does earth mean here? | A wire | *Soil, the ground plants grow in | The sky | The planet
exercise: A person who is «down to earth» is what? | From another planet | Able to fly | *Sensible and practical | Living under the ground
test: How often does Earth spin? | Once a week | *Once a day | Once a year | Never
test: What is the best way to check which meaning of earth fits a sentence? | Count the letters | *Swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense | Skip the sentence forever | Look only at the first letter
exam: Which sentence uses earth to mean the planet? | *«Each person has one life on this earth.» | «Ukraine's black earth is about a metre deep.» | «Plants need rich earth to grow.» | «He dug a hole deep into the earth.»
